-- Upper Karazhan Halls (map 814): Anomalus, the Echo of Medivh, Incantagos, Keeper Gnarlmoon, the Kings' Council, Kruul and Sanv Tas'dal: its C++ as rows -- EPIC10 tier 2.
-- Written by the trt repo's scripts/tier2/a17_upper_karazhan_halls.py from d6_world; upper_karazhan_halls_restore.sql puts
-- back what this replaces. R8: a person applies it, into the world database.
--
-- The C++ keeps its script names: mod-upper-karazhan-halls is the switch (AM1, handoff/manager-091).
-- Loaded, the C++ runs as before -- a script found by name comes first. Unloaded
-- (`module unload mod-upper-karazhan-halls`, which gives every creature standing a new AI at once),
-- the names find no script and the creatures run these rows (their ai_name).
--
-- Anomalus's timers shorten in four health bands, 0.87, 0.62, 0.39 and 0.3 of the C++'s 15/24/9 s (the C++ scaled
-- each re-arm by max(30, health %) / 100; a band's factor gives its cast count), a later band's first cast anywhere
-- in its interval; his target is a random player who is not his victim and under none of his three debuffs (the
-- C++ took the first such on the threat list). The Echo's Medivh's Fury comes once per 15 s while four stacks of
-- Guardian's Ire hold, Ire's own duration (the C++ cast it on every interrupt at four or more; no condition reads
-- a stack count); his spells come one per 500 ms between casts (the C++ chose one each tick). Incantagos's watchers
-- carry a mark (22805, a dummy aura used nowhere else) in place of the C++'s guids, and his charge is counted from
-- the marked alive within 100 yd; a watcher that evades alone loses the mark (the C++ kept its guid); a watcher
-- dead in phase 2 keeps phase 2 (the C++ dropped to 0 or 1 and yelled its 40 % line again). Gnarlmoon's moons fall
-- by a coin per player (the C++ gave the first half the Red Moon); the intermission ends when no owl is left alive
-- (the C++ counted four deaths); 66.6 and 33.3 % are 66 and 33 %. The Bishop's Redemption rises every dead Pawn
-- within 40 yd (the C++ the nearest). The Rook's and the Knight's faster-alone timers are rules of their own, so the
-- first cast after the pieces fall comes at once. Kruul's enraged Mark and Call first come 15 s after the enrage
-- (the C++ carried their phase-0 countdowns over, 0-30 and 0-25 s left: 15 s is the nearest fixed time); his Mark
-- may pick a player twice (the C++ three distinct); his swing animation with Remorseless Strikes is dropped. The
-- DEBUG yells of Gnarlmoon and Sanv Tas'dal are dropped.

